  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Getting to ZERO TB Deaths in Zimbabwe: Intensifying efforts to Find, Treat and Cure all TB Cases - Zimbabwe (01-Jan-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe, Tuberculosis, The Ministry of Health and Child Care of the Republic of Zimbabwe (MOHCC)This program has the following goals: By 2025 to have reduced mortality of all forms of TB by 80% from 132/100000 in 2012 to 26/100 000.  By 2025 to have reduced the incidence of all forms of TB by 80% from 562/100000 in 2012 to 112/100 000. The objectives of this program are: To increase case notification rate of all forms of tuberculosis from 288/100 000 (35,278 patients) in 2013 to 377/100 000 (52060 patients) by 2017..  To increase the number of DR-TB cases detected annually from 625 in 2013 to 990 in 2017.  To increase treatment success rate for all forms of tuberculosis from 81% in 2012 to 90% by 2017.  To increase treatment success rate of Drug resistance TB from 59% in 2011 to 75% in 2017</narrative>
  </description>
